  "keyboard": [
    {
      "keys": ["Tab", "Shift+Tab"],
      "effect": "Moves the focus into the field and on to the next or the previous control. A disabled field is skipped."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Enter"],
      "effect": "Starts a new line. It never sends the form: a text area's form is sent by its submit button."
    }
  ],
  "aria": {
    "pattern": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-textarea-element",
    "rules": [
      "It is a native textarea element, with its `rows`, and an autocomplete where the browser can fill it in.",
      "The label is a label element for the text area: its accessible name.",
      "The help and the error are its description, by `aria-describedby`. While the error shows it takes the help's place.",
      "A field in error has `aria-invalid` true. Its error says how to fix it, and is never a color alone: it has its word and its icon.",
      "A required field has the required attribute, which assistive technology reads; the asterisk shows it.",
      "A disabled field is the native disabled attribute."
    ]
  },
  "forcedColors": [
    "The edge is a real border, which forced colors keep in the system's colors, and in `GrayText` when the field is disabled.",
    "The focus ring is an outline, which forced colors keep.",
    "The error icon takes the system's text color, as the error's word does, so both still say it is an error."
  ],
  "motion": [
    "The edge changes color in `motion.duration.fast`, with `motion.easing.standard`. With `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` it changes at once."
  ],
  "content": [
    "The label names the text, in sentence case and with no colon: Message, Notes for the organizer.",
    "No placeholders. What to write goes in the help under the field: Up to 500 characters.",
    "An error says how to fix it, not only what is wrong: Shorten the message to 500 characters or fewer."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Its height is not a row of the table: it is as tall as its rows of text, by the `rows` attribute, three unless the text is known to be longer, and an implementation may grow it as the reader types.",
    "Its first line sits where an input's value does: the padding above and below the text is half of what the control's height leaves around a line, less the edge, so a text area of one row is as tall as the input of its size.",
    "It has no icons and no loading state, unlike the input: an icon beside several lines of text has no one line to sit on.",
    "Read-only is not specced: a value that cannot be changed, as on a review step, is shown as a term and its value, with `ws-pairs`.",
    "A hint beside the label is not part of the spec: hints go under the field, as its help.",
    "The text keeps its place when the edge widens: an invalid field's padding on every side is its padding at rest less the extra edge, `control.border-width.invalid` less `control.border-width.rest`, so its edge grows inward over the padding and nothing in the box moves."
  ],
